    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to present 121 Hunters Green to the market. A superb two bedroom duplex which exudes quality and is situated in the ever popular Hunterswood development. Immaculately presented throughout, this two bedroom duplex is perfectly suited for first time buyers, investors or those looking to downsize A superb home in an unrivalled location. The well-proportioned accommodation that is excellently designed with comfortable living in mind briefly comprises; entrance hall with excellent guest wc, large open plan kitchen/living/dining room. Upstairs there are two spacious double bedrooms (master en-suite) with a family bathroom completing the accommodation. The property is further enhanced by a low maintenance terrace to the front and a beautiful communal green as well as the added bonus of having an allocated parking space along with ample visitor parking. Hunterswood enjoys the benefits of an idyllic setting at the foothills of the Dublin Mountains. This sought-after development has beautiful landscaped communal areas and enjoys the best of both worlds - village life close to the city, and is minutes from an abundance of well-established amenities such as Marley Park and St Enda's Park, sports facilities, libraries and restaurants in the Knocklyon, Templeogue and Rathfarnham area. Early viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 2.05m x 4.57m\nWelcoming entrance hall with tiled flooring and attractive glass panels either side of the front door, creating a bright and spacious first impression.\n\nGuest WC/Utility - 2.05m x 1.50m\nConvenient guest WC with tiled flooring, WC and wash hand basin. The room is also plumbed for a washing machine and benefits from excellent additional storage, with generous presses located behind closed doors.\n\nLiving/Dining/Kitchen - 4.06m x 6.08m\nA superb open-plan living, dining and kitchen area providing a bright and versatile space for both everyday living. The living and dining area features beautiful solid timber flooring, while Rationale-style patio doors open directly onto the southerly-facing patio area. The patio is exceptionally private and provides a lovely extension of the living space.The kitchen has a tiled floor and tiled splashback and is fitted with a good range of floor and eye-level units, with excellent storage. A breakfast bar provides additional seating and incorporates further storage beneath. The kitchen is equipped with an integrated dishwasher, oven, hob, extractor fan and integrated fridge freezer.\n\nMaster Bedroom - 2.80m x 4.24m\nExceptionally bright and spacious double bedroom with laminate timber flooring and excellent built-in wardrobe storage. The room benefits from a generous layout and excellent natural light.\n\nEn-Suite Shower Room - 1.67m x 1.69m\nFully fitted en-suite shower room comprising WC, wash hand basin and shower cubicle with glass shower enclosure.\n\nBedroom Two - 3.28m x 3.11m\nA second bright and well-proportioned double bedroom with laminate timber flooring and built-in wardrobes, providing excellent storage.\n\nBathroom - 2.30m x 1.69m\nThe main bathroom comprises WC, wash hand basin, fitted mirror and bath with shower attachment.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Electric storage heaters</li><li>Cable TV</li><li>Broadband</li><li>1 designated parking space in carport. </li><li>Management company: Hunterswood Management company</li><li>Management fee: 1,258pa</ul>"
      },
